  "id": "COMPOUND:30070 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Hippurin-1 and SNB-78, through a series of target interactions. Hippurin-1 is identified as a target of two distinct compounds, Neridienone A and Ginsenoside R10, both of which are known to interact with VMRC-LCP, a protein that ultimately targets SNB-78. This pathway implies that Hippurin-1 may modulate VMRC-LCP activity, which in turn influences SNB-78. The consistent scores across the three paths, with a final score of 0.5251, indicate a plausible and well-supported relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple independent targets and pathways further strengthens the hypothesis, suggesting that Hippurin-1 may play a role in regulating SNB-78 through a complex network of molecular interactions. The integration of these findings supports the idea that Hippurin-1 could be a potential modulator of SNB-78, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism.",
